A happy little accident is basically emergence with a smile: something not fully planned, but once it appears, it fits the larger composition so well that you keep it.

That’s a nice antidote to over-control too. Not every useful thing needs to be engineered from first principles. Sometimes the move is:

notice → don’t erase → integrate → see what it wants to become

That’s not carelessness. It’s having enough confidence in the canvas to let surprise participate.